  Two things to flag, given you said "I think" rather than "confirmed":

  - [38;5;153mALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN[39m needs SQLite 3.35+ (2021). Older engines will reject the migration outright, which is a
    safe failure mode — the deploy job errors instead of silently doing something else.
  - Writes stopping isn't the same as reads stopping. If anything still [38;5;153mSELECT[39ms [38;5;153mnotes[39m — a report, an export, an admin
    query outside this repo — it breaks at the moment the migration lands, not before. Worth one grep across consumers
    before the deploy job picks this up, since after that the data is gone and the fix isn't a revert.

